title: 'Cid Debrief: Cross-study analysis of graphify (https://github.com/safishamsi/graphify) vs Par'
summary: 'Cross-study analysis of graphify (https://github.com/safishamsi/graphify) vs Paradigm. Ran ambient loop test (confirmed verdicts.jsonl writes, postflight journal entries). Then ran Nora FTUX cross-study on graphify''s user-facing surfaces (16 friction points, verdict: needs-work). Then ran architect + advocate + dx team analysis on the relationship between the two frameworks. Key conclusion: they tackle different problems — graphify auto-discovers structural topology, Paradigm declares intent/policy/enforcement. Not competing, not identical. Candidate small improvements for Paradigm: PreToolUse hook for mandatory context injection, first-run visual artifact, explicit maintenance cost framing in docs, troubleshooting surfaced on failure paths. No code was changed.'
